{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"title":"How-to Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Cancel Effects"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","isActive":true},{"text":" and the store’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all-or-nothing"}]},{"text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cancel id"}]},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true},{"text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"text":" effect or the imperative ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"text":" method. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"text":" carries cancellation metadata alongside its async operation. The store registers declared cancellation scopes synchronously before starting background work, so an immediate cancellation cannot race registration.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Choosing an id","type":"heading","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A cancel id is any ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable & Sendable"},{"text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["private struct SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private struct SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","type":"heading","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Return ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" to tag the work, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"text":" to stop it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancellation is cooperative: a stream or service must observe cancellation to stop its work. Keyed effects also suppress sends after cancellation, so a service that returns a stale successful result cannot publish it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","type":"heading","anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Passing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancelInFlight: true"},{"text":" cancels any effect already running under the id ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches "},{"code":".queryChanged","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Cancel from view or scene code","type":"heading","anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" directly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What it does not replace","type":"heading","anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an "},{"code":"AsyncStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" continuation should still release it — use "},{"code":"withTaskCancellationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defer"},{"type":"text","text":". Cancellation requests that the task stop; it does not close what the task opened."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" has to stop the effect early."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Constructing and lifting effects","type":"heading","anchor":"Constructing-and-lifting-effects","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create ordinary work with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Effect { send in ... }"},{"type":"text","text":". When a feature returns an effect with its own action type, lift it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["return featureEffect.map(AppAction.feature)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" preserves cancellation metadata. Wrapping another effect inside a new operation hides that declaration from the store until the inner effect is invoked. Such dynamically invoked scopes become active on invocation; cancelling an ID does not prohibit future scopes with that ID. Scope registrations are removed when their operation finishes, including when it throws. Cancellation keys are not retained as a history of past commands."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swidux","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","kind":"article","title":"Add Feature Flags","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancel(id:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/cancel(id:)","abstract":[{"text":"Cancels every in-flight effect tagged with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" via","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"cancel(id:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":" & "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","kind":"symbol","title":"Effect","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Async work with cancellation metadata declared before the store starts it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","kind":"article","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","abstract":[{"text":"Install the bundled ","type":"text"},{"code":"swidux-ref","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","kind":"article","title":"Add Persistence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","kind":"article","title":"Add a Parental Gate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","kind":"article","title":"Add iCloud Sync","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","kind":"symbol","title":"cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancellable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancelInFlight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Send","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux4Senda"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6EffectV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Tags an effect with a cancellation identity so it can later be cancelled by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.cancel(id:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelinflight:_:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","kind":"article","title":"Add a Version Killswitch","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkills